+
+
+## Completed-DMA software AEC laboratory variant
+
+The separate `m5stack-stopwatch-software-aec` build keeps these pins and mono
+ES8311 hardware unchanged. It selects USB Serial/JTAG as the primary console,
+starts in local observation/ordinary cloud auto mode, and requires an explicit
+`aec_realtime on` command after readiness and operator measurements. It is not
+acoustically accepted firmware. The normal `m5stack-stopwatch` variant is retained.
+
+```sh
+python3 scripts/build.py m5stack/stopwatch --name m5stack-stopwatch-software-aec --zip
+```
+
+Local commands: `aec_stats`, `aec_diag_start <RFC1918-IPv4> <port> <seconds>`,
+`aec_diag_stop`, `aec_realtime on`, `aec_realtime off`. Capture is off by default,
+duration is1..120 seconds, and datagrams use the versioned `SWAC` header defined
+in the owning integration repository's `firmware/README.md`. No audio files are
+stored on the device. `CONFIG_STOPWATCH_AEC_OFFSET_SAMPLES` is a bounded calibration
+setting; completion timestamps do not establish acoustic alignment. This variant
+requires `CONFIG_I2S_ISR_IRAM_SAFE=n` and exact ESP-IDF6.1/esp_codec_dev1.6.2 source.
